From 829ea6de559ea9ed51d9fba5fa248982ca50c2ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usman Akram <102724070+UsmaNaman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:14:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nv2a/vk: replace guest textures from an RRL texture pack

When XEMU_TEXTURE_PACK_DIR is set, a non-linear, non-indexed 2D texture
whose content hash has <hash>.rgba in that directory is created from the
file instead: "RRT1", LE u32 width/height/levels, then RGBA8 levels. The
size must be the guest size times a power of two; sampler min/max LOD
are shifted by that power so the game's mip clamps still apply. A
replaced binding whose content changes is rebuilt, since its image size
and format differ from the guest shape. The staging-to-image copy is
split out of upload_texture_image so both paths share it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZfY8PfkRfJCjArnYegSSy
